{"cluster_id": "C-1745", "topic": "The pre-fold drain takes a complete catalog snapshot, selects one eligib", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-025"], "canonical_claim": "The pre-fold drain takes a complete catalog snapshot, selects one eligible row, and restarts its complete scan after every CAS outcome; only a scan with no eligible row permits the invocation to continue.", "issue_ids": ["r9-6"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1746", "topic": "The dead-life janitor enumerates `cas/ns/` separately from the fold's ho", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-031"], "canonical_claim": "The dead-life janitor enumerates `cas/ns/` separately from the fold's hot `cas/ns/stream/` LIST, takes one fresh catalog GET per page rather than per key, and deletes only after page-wide life revalidation and an exact fence/token check.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1747", "topic": "Janitor progress is stored in the leak-only `<prefix>/gc/maintenance_sta", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-032"], "canonical_claim": "Janitor progress is stored in the leak-only `<prefix>/gc/maintenance_state` object registered as `FormatId::GcMaintenanceState = 25`; losing or repeating this cursor can repeat cleanup work or leak bytes, but cannot affect GC authority, frontier completeness, `DEFER`, catalog lifecycle, or successor publication.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1748", "topic": "A physical id returned by a completed LIST and absent from the correspon", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-037"], "canonical_claim": "A physical id returned by a completed LIST and absent from the corresponding later catalog cut is inert dead-life debris: the fold counts and drops it, while only the janitor may nominate its physical deletion.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1749", "topic": "snapshot-checkpoint-deletion", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-047", "B027-131", "B037-059"], "canonical_claim": "Snapshots are deletable only strictly below `_ckpt.checkpoint`; a stale pointer can only under-clean, and a missing sampled base requires rereading `_ckpt` to distinguish a concurrent advancement from corruption. Additionally, Snapshots are deletable only strictly below `checkpoint_snapshot_id`; if a sampled checkpoint base is missing, a changed `_ckpt` token causes restart and an unchanged token causes `CORRUPTED_DATA`. Additionally, Snapshot cleanup may delete only snapshots strictly below the current `_ckpt` base; deleting the snapshot still named by `ckpt.base` must fail closed as corruption after exact-key revalidation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaRefTableSnapshotLogCore_RESULTS.md#L206-L213", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-5", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1750", "topic": "After the mandatory pre-fold drain, the fold performs one strict `LIST(c", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-057"], "canonical_claim": "After the mandatory pre-fold drain, the fold performs one strict `LIST(cas/ns/stream/)`, then one fresh full-catalog cut, and builds its sole ref plan from that cut plus the completed LIST observations.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#fold"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1751", "topic": "arithmetic-ref-log-walk", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-058", "B027-136", "B029-027", "B034-017", "B036-020"], "canonical_claim": "Each catalog-admitted life is folded arithmetically from its adopted cursor through exact `_ckpt.committed_through`; an omitted life receives the same finite exact walk, while hint holes such as `0x1430c`/`0x1430d` are not correctness gaps. Additionally, Fold arithmetic intake walks exact `expected = cursor + 1` keys rather than iterating `listing.logs`; a hint hole that GET finds is folded without anomaly, while a 404 with no higher witness marks the normal frontier. Additionally, The GC fold reads `expected = cursor + 1` by exact key, proves epoch crossings via `crossFromSeal`, treats a hint hole as a non-event, and turns an absent expected-next with a witness above it into a per-namespace HOLD with `ShardCoverage::classification == 4`. Additionally, The middle of a ref-log enumeration remains arithmetic on every backend because predecessor omission below a correct paginated LIST tail is legal under concurrent writes; held namespaces and namespaces with no listed logs must still use the probe. Additionally, The ref-log intake walk still issues the exact-key `GET` at `cursor + 1` even when `cursor == tail`; an absent expected-next key with no higher witness is the proof that sets `frontier_proven`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-stage-a-retirement-verdicts.md#probe-a", "docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#gc-frontier-one-list", "docs/superpowers/models/CaGcRootLocalPartManifestCore_RESULTS.md#verdict-listedtok-skip-premise-retired", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-7", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#fold"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1752", "topic": "A destructive round may perform condemnation, graduation, deletion, swee", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-059"], "canonical_claim": "A destructive round may perform condemnation, graduation, deletion, sweep deletes, or ref cleanup only after every `Live`/`Removing` catalog entry reaches its same-round `_ckpt.committed_through` frontier; missing checkpoints, incomplete walks, or budget exhaustion suppress all destruction.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#fold"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1753", "topic": "A manifest from epoch E is deletable only after the cursor consumes epoc", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-064"], "canonical_claim": "A manifest from epoch E is deletable only after the cursor consumes epoch E's seal and no unconsumed tail record above the cursor names it as a removal target; any uncertainty retains it.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#sweep"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1754", "topic": "mandatory-catalog-frontier-targets", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-116", "B037-116"], "canonical_claim": "Stage A hard-wires `frontier_incomplete = true` through `UniversePolicy::kDefault = StageA_Suppressed`, so `suppress_destructive` holds on every production round and all delete families remain inert until Stage B supplies the catalog universe. Additionally, The pool-wide ref-delta fold makes every catalog `Live`/`Removing` life a mandatory target, snapshots exact `_ckpt.committed_through`, walks arithmetically to that bound, and treats every missing required key as a durable hold independent of `LIST`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/README.md#group-ref-table", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#staging-contract"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1755", "topic": "Epochs are crossed only by consuming a seal at the expected id", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-137"], "canonical_claim": "Epochs are crossed only by consuming a seal at the expected id; an `EpochSeal` is counted as applied with `produced=false`, and a later-epoch record reachable before its seal is held rather than guessed across.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-7"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1756", "topic": "Per-namespace fold failures such as corrupt bodies clamp or hold that na", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-138"], "canonical_claim": "Per-namespace fold failures such as corrupt bodies clamp or hold that namespace, while the rest of the round continues; only a key unattributable to any namespace aborts the whole round.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-7"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1757", "topic": "classification-four-hold-fields", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-139", "B041-057"], "canonical_claim": "`ShardCoverage` classification 4 requires `HoldReason`, `offending_position`, `retry_count`, and `next_retry_round`, and those fields are forbidden for other classifications; malformed hold grammar is `CORRUPTED_DATA`. Additionally, Classification 4 requires bounded hold fields and forbids those fields for other classifications; unknown, duplicate, or invalid field combinations must be rejected.", "issue_ids": ["r9-4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-8", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r8_findings.md#L72-L78"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1758", "topic": "hold-clear-after-adoption", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-140", "B041-051"], "canonical_claim": "A hold clears only after folding through its `offending_position` and adopting the result in `gc/state`; if an above-cursor witness disappears while the gap remains, the hold changes to `WitnessDisappeared` and remains held. Additionally, A successful frontier walk clears a hold only when folding through the offending position and adopting that result in gc/state; reaching another absent expected-next does not clear it.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-8", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r8_findings.md#L20-L26"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1759", "topic": "frontier-exact-get-and-budget", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-141", "B041-035"], "canonical_claim": "The fold's `DestructiveGate` requires a frontier proof for every known namespace; a quiet namespace is probed with one exact GET of `expected_next(cursor)`, and budget exhaustion suppresses all destruction even if safe cursor progress is published. Additionally, Every destructive round must exact-GET cursor+1 for every Live or Removing catalog entry and suppress all destructive work if the common budget expires before every namespace has a frontier proof.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-9", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_r7_findings.md#L15-L17"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1760", "topic": "manifest-deletion-premise", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B027-145", "B029-004"], "canonical_claim": "The sweep's shared `manifestDeletionPremise` requires both consumption of the manifest's epoch seal and no unconsumed tail removal target; unreached frontier, budget exhaustion, or a hold retains the manifest. Additionally, The orphan-manifest sweep deletes only with seal-consumed and no-tail-removal evidence; when the evidence is uncertain, it retains the object.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-stage-a-RESULTS.md#aggregate-posture", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-10"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1761", "topic": "The hot GC round completes one `LIST(cas/ns/stream/)`, then takes one au", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-020"], "canonical_claim": "The hot GC round completes one `LIST(cas/ns/stream/)`, then takes one authoritative full-catalog `{token, value}` cut; `Live` and `Removing` entries in that cut are admitted, while listed ids absent from the later cut are inert dead-life debris and are not admitted or a reason to defer.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-4d"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1762", "topic": "pre-fold-drain-and-fresh-cut", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-022", "B037-006", "B037-034", "B037-118"], "canonical_claim": "Every GC invocation acquires and validates the lease and adopted seal, conclusively drains eligible `Removing` rows, completes `LIST(cas/ns/stream/)`, takes one fresh full-catalog cut, builds the ref walk plan, and only then decides `DEFER` or performs fold, seal, and adoption. Additionally, Before any fold, `REBUILD`, or `DEFER` decision, the production GC actor must read the currently adopted parent seal, drain every eligible catalog row, conclusively resolve every exact CAS, and take a fresh catalog cut. Additionally, Before `DEFER`, ordinary fold adoption, or `REBUILD` adoption, GC actor B must read the authoritative parent, resolve every eligible exact catalog CAS, complete the hot-stream `LIST`, take one fresh authoritative catalog cut, and build the ref-walk plan. Additionally, A pre-fold GC invocation must resolve all eligible exact catalog CAS operations, complete hot `LIST`, take one fresh cut, and build the sole ref plan before fold, `REBUILD`, or `DEFER`; ambiguous results cannot be treated as completion.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/CaRefCatalogCore_RESULTS.md#L60-L63", "docs/superpowers/models/CaRefPreFoldDrainCore_RESULTS.md#caref-prefolddraincore-results", "docs/superpowers/models/README.md#group-ref-table", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1763", "topic": "A complete `Removing` row may be exact-CAS-deleted only when the matchin", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-023"], "canonical_claim": "A complete `Removing` row may be exact-CAS-deleted only when the matching adopted parent life row contains cleanup evidence and no durable hold; ambiguous or conflicting catalog CAS outcomes are resolved conclusively before successor publication.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-5"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1764", "topic": "namespace-janitor-page", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-026", "B032-021"], "canonical_claim": "The perpetual janitor scans `LIST(cas/ns/)` in bounded pages, stores one cleanup-only opaque pagination token in `GcMaintenanceState`, and takes a fresh catalog read after each page before classifying and exact-token-deleting candidates. Additionally, The perpetual `NamespaceJanitor::runOnePage` is invoked every GC round, is bounded by `page_budget`, is fenced by `gc/state` lease owner and sequence, and is leak-only.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-stage-b-midpoint-audit.md#t5-3-code-obligations-at-head", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-5-step-8"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1765", "topic": "Destructive cleanup of a current catalog life revalidates the life and f", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-033"], "canonical_claim": "Destructive cleanup of a current catalog life revalidates the life and fence immediately before every per-key `deleteExact`; the dead-life janitor may use a page-level catalog cut because catalog-before-object publication and non-reused `life_id` provide the stronger ordering proof.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-6"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1766", "topic": "In the fold model, a page scan is only a hint that may omit keys", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-045"], "canonical_claim": "In the fold model, a page scan is only a hint that may omit keys; arithmetic `WalkStep` advances the cursor by expected transaction id and supplies the authoritative delta candidates.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-tla-phase.md#L124-L180"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1767", "topic": "The fold's blob in-degree is pool-wide and is computed from fixed `EdgeO", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-046"], "canonical_claim": "The fold's blob in-degree is pool-wide and is computed from fixed `EdgeOf` roles over folded keys; condemnation requires every table frontier proof and no hold, while deletion also requires no hold and two-phase pacing.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-tla-phase.md#L124-L180"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1768", "topic": "The stale-leader cleanup model makes recreation safe structurally", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B028-049"], "canonical_claim": "The stale-leader cleanup model makes recreation safe structurally: stale deletes capture and target the old incarnation, while reuse of an incarnation is the sabotage that violates rebirth safety.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-tla-phase.md#L224-L241"]}
