{"cluster_id": "C-1770", "topic": "A 404 while folding a body the round already decided to read is treated ", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B029-028"], "canonical_claim": "A 404 while folding a body the round already decided to read is treated as a concurrent delete and recorded while the round continues; this behavior remains required because throwing would wedge GC for the pool.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-07-28-stage-a-retirement-verdicts.md#404"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1771", "topic": "`CaGcAckFloorCore`, `CaGcAckFloorZombie`, and `CaGcCondemnMarkerGate` as", "target": "architecture/garbage-collection", "member_ids": ["B029-038"], "canonical_claim": "`CaGcAckFloorCore`, `CaGcAckFloorZombie`, and `CaGcCondemnMarkerGate` assume a complete fold cut; v9 turns that assumption into arithmetic discovery plus a durable classification-4 hold, so an undeclared skipped suffix becomes structurally unrepresentable without rewriting those orthogonal models.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/models/2026-07-28-v9-phase-RESULTS.md#audit-complete-cut"]}

